      "id": "allahakbarries",
      "name": "Allahakbarries",
      "founded": 1887,
      "dissolved": 1913,
      "founder": "J.M. Barrie",
      "type": "writers",
      "description": "J.M. Barrie's celebrated team of literary amateurs, named in the mistaken belief that 'Allah akbar' meant 'Heaven help us' — appropriate enough for a side whose enthusiasm reliably outran its competence. Played friendlies across England and on the lawns of country houses for a quarter-century, fielding what now reads as a who's-who of late-Victorian and Edwardian letters.",
      "sources": [
        "Kevin Telfer, Peter Pan's First XI: The Extraordinary Story of J.M. Barrie's Cricket Team (2010)",
        "J.M. Barrie, Allahakbarrie Book of Broadway Cricket (1899)"
      ],
