      "type": "theatrical",
      "description": "The Gaieties were founded by the music-hall comedian Lupino Lane in 1937, and have been the central institution of theatrical and literary cricket ever since. Harold Pinter was Chairman from 1972 until his death in 2008, ferocious in the field and, latterly, unsparing in the umpire's coat. Tom Stoppard is reported by Hermione Lee to have kept wicket. The club still plays out of grounds across London and the home counties.",
